We have to specify the type of values explicitly to construct `List<Decimal>`, otherwise it will always going to take `Decimal(32, 32)`. Because we have:

```rust
impl From<PrimitiveType> for ArrowDataType {
    fn from(item: PrimitiveType) -> Self {
        match item {
            // ......
            PrimitiveType::Int128 => ArrowDataType::Decimal(32, 32),
        }
    }
}
```

As a result, the `precision and scale` of the underlying array doesn't match `ChunkedArray`, which can produce unexpected results when we cast.
